{"patch":{"config":{"title":"Antranig Basman","baseURL":"https://ponder.org.uk","defaultContentLanguage":"en","mainSections":["post","posts"],"author":{"name":"Antranig Basman","website":"/","email":"amb26web@ponder.org.uk","twitter":"amb26ponder"},"params":{"homeTitle":"Antranig Basman","subtitle":"Building habitable technologies","bio":"img/20230209_135356 - bio - cropped.jpg","logo":"img/pond.jpg","favicon":"img/favicon.ico","dateFormat":"January 2, 2006","comments":true,"socialShare":true,"showRelatedPosts":true,"commentsLayer":"beautifulWend.comments.giscus","customCSS":["css/ponder.css"],"mediaIcons":[{"title":"Twitter profile","href":"http://twitter.com/amb26ponder","icon":"fab fa-twitter"},{"title":"Send me a message","href":"mailto:amb26webpage@ponder.org.uk","icon":"fa fa-envelope"},{"title":"Antranig's GitHub profile","href":"http://github.com/amb26","icon":"fab fa-github-alt"},{"title":"My papers on DBLP","href":"https://dblp.org/pid/68/5013.html","icon":"fa fa-university"},{"title":"My LinkedIn profile","href":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/antranigbasman/","icon":"fab fa-linkedin"}],"giscus":{"repo":"amb26/ponder","repoId":"R_kgDOOKllGA","category":"Announcements","categoryId":"DIC_kwDOOKllGM4CvhAS"}},"menu":{"main":[{"name":"Posts","url":"post","weight":1},{"name":"WiP","url":"wip","weight":1},{"name":"Docs","identifier":"docs","url":"docs","weight":3},{"name":"Fluid Signals","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-signals","weight":1},{"name":"Fluid Integration Language","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-integration-language","weight":2},{"name":"Fluid View","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-view","weight":3},{"name":"Fluid PTF","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-ptf","weight":4},{"name":"Fluid tldraw integration","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-tldraw","weight":5},{"name":"wend","parent":"docs","url":"docs/wend","weight":6},{"name":"About","url":"page/about/","weight":3},{"name":"Communities","url":"communities","weight":4},{"name":"Projects","url":"projects","weight":5},{"name":"Terms","url":"term","weight":5}]}},"features":{"selfHosted":true,"hljs":true,"katex":false}},"pages":[{"kind":"page","type":"infusion-docs","section":"docs","title":"wend","relPermalink":"/docs/wend/","permalink":"https://ponder.org.uk/docs/wend/","outputPath":"/docs/wend/index.html","params":{"title":"wend","category":"Infusion","type":"infusion-docs"},"sourcePath":"content/docs/wend.md","content":"<p>Wend builds a static site from Infusion 6 components, and lets the site be edited in place, in the browser,\nwith the edits committed to its GitHub repository. This site is built with it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"edit-in-infusion\"><a class=\"infusion-docs-anchor\" aria-label=\"Edit in Infusion\" href=\"#edit-in-infusion\"><span class=\"octicon octicon-link\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></a>Edit in Infusion</h2>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://github.com/fluid-project/infusion-6/releases/latest/download/edit-in-infusion.zip\">Download the latest Edit in Infusion extension (zip)</a></strong></p>\n<p>“Edit in Infusion” is the Chrome extension which makes a wend site editable in place: edit a page as it is shown, or\nits markdown source beside it, and commit the edits to the site’s repository. See its\n<a href=\"/edit-in-infusion-privacy/\">privacy policy</a>.</p>\n<p>Earlier versions are among the <a href=\"https://github.com/fluid-project/infusion-6/releases\">releases</a> of Infusion’s\nrepository. To install it from the zip:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Unzip it into a directory of its own.</li>\n<li>Open <code>chrome://extensions</code> in Chrome, and turn on <strong>Developer mode</strong>, at the top right.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Load unpacked</strong>, and choose the directory.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>You can also install the most recent published version from the <a href=\"https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/edit-in-infusion/epphpgiplmpablplnonaihjhfmkhcimn\">Chrome Extension Store</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"packages\"><a class=\"infusion-docs-anchor\" aria-label=\"Packages\" href=\"#packages\"><span class=\"octicon octicon-link\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></a>Packages</h2>\n<p>wend is published to npm from <a href=\"https://github.com/fluid-project/infusion-6\">Infusion 6’s repository</a>, in two packages:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@fluid-project/wend\"><code>@fluid-project/wend</code></a> - the build, run as <code>wend-build</code> in the site’s directory, and what is\npublished for editing in place.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@fluid-project/wend-theme-beautiful\"><code>@fluid-project/wend-theme-beautiful</code></a> - a theme, the page furniture of\nBeautiful Hugo as Infusion 6 layers, which this site uses.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A site describes itself to wend by its <code>wend.site.json</code> - its modules, its host document, its editing configuration\nand its static directories. See wend’s\n<a href=\"https://github.com/fluid-project/infusion-6/tree/main/packages/wend\">README</a> for the details.</p>\n","summary":"Wend builds a static site from Infusion 6 components, and lets the site be edited in place, in the browser, with the edits committed to its GitHub repository. This site is built with it. Edit in Infusion Download the latest Edit in Infusion extension (zip) “Edit in Infusion” is the Chrome extension which makes a wend site editable in place: edit a page as it is shown, or its markdown source beside it, and commit the edits to the site’s repository.","summaryText":"Wend builds a static site from Infusion 6 components, and lets the site be edited in place, in the browser, with the edits committed to its GitHub repository. This site is built with it. Edit in Infusion Download the latest Edit in Infusion extension (zip) “Edit in Infusion” is the Chrome extension which makes a wend site editable in place: edit a page as it is shown, or its markdown source beside it, and commit the edits to the site’s repository.","truncated":true,"nextInSection":{"title":"Layer Linearisation","relPermalink":"/docs/linearisation-algorithm/"}}],"shared":{"lang":"en","menu":[{"name":"Posts","url":"post","weight":1,"children":[]},{"name":"WiP","url":"wip","weight":1,"children":[]},{"name":"About","url":"page/about/","weight":3,"children":[]},{"name":"Docs","identifier":"docs","url":"docs","weight":3,"children":[{"name":"Fluid Signals","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-signals","weight":1,"children":[]},{"name":"Fluid Integration Language","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-integration-language","weight":2,"children":[]},{"name":"Fluid View","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-view","weight":3,"children":[]},{"name":"Fluid PTF","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-ptf","weight":4,"children":[]},{"name":"Fluid tldraw integration","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-tldraw","weight":5,"children":[]},{"name":"wend","parent":"docs","url":"docs/wend","weight":6,"children":[]}]},{"name":"Communities","url":"communities","weight":4,"children":[]},{"name":"Projects","url":"projects","weight":5,"children":[]},{"name":"Terms","url":"term","weight":5,"children":[]}],"buildYear":2026,"relatedIndex":[{"relPermalink":"/","title":"Antranig Basman","kind":"home","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/post/","title":"post","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/wip/","title":"wip","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/wip/page/2/","title":"wip","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/docs/","title":"docs","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/page/","title":"page","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/term/","title":"term","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/term/page/2/","title":"term","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/post/2026-06-28-fully-deferred-stabilization/","title":"Bridging the gap between static and dynamic analysis through fully deferred stabilization","kind":"page","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/wip/2026-05-25-towards-deferred-stabilisation/","title":"Towards Deferred Stabilisation","kind":"page","params":{}}